Z||000000||baptistheart||09-24-2001||04:53 PM||||My car has feul up to the injector,The wires going to the injector are hot(tbi injector). I havent had time to check spark. If their is no spark could this be the control module?<P>i'v checked the comp. it's working. don't know what else to look for.<P>------------------<BR>Joe||||reg||5
Z||000001||Steve Normington||09-24-2001||06:47 PM||||Could be the control module. Take it to an auto parts store and they should be able to test it.<P>[Edit]Is it the DIS or distributor system? DIS could be the crank pickup. Put an voltmeter on AC on the wires out the pickup. If you don't get about 1-2V when cranking the engine, it may be bad. If distributor, it could be the pickup coil. Also check the coil(s) for proper restiance. .5 - .95 (?) for the primary, 5K - 7K ohms (?) for the secondary.<p>[This message has been edited by Steve Normington (edited 09-24-2001).]||||reg||1
